{
  "id": "COMPOUND:43011 - PROTEIN:4915",
  "verbalization": "Mangostenone D appears to have a direct interaction with Replicase polyprotein 1ab through multiple distinct targets, all of which are involved in the life cycle of the virus that replicates the replicase polyprotein. The evidence suggests that Mangostenone D acts as a broad-spectrum inhibitor of viral replication, targeting different viral proteins that are essential for the assembly and function of the replicase polyprotein. These targets include SNU-387, a compound that is a known target of Mangostenone D, and other related compounds such as Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside and 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, which are also implicated in the viral replication process. The presence of multiple targets indicates that Mangostenone D may exert its antiviral effects through a variety of mechanisms, potentially involving the inhibition of viral protein synthesis or the disruption of viral assembly. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Mangostenone D may act as a potent antiviral agent by targeting the replicase polyprotein, thereby interfering with the viral replication cycle.",
